Concern: wrappers that attach each printed path's first-line annotation to another tool's output, and the PreToolUse injector that routes an agent to them | Non-concern: running the wrapped tool (the agent's own shell does), the annotation grammar and charter resolution (the annotated-tree library owns both), and everything SPEC.md governs | IO: (producer argv, that tool's output on stdin, hook JSON) -> the same output with contracts appended, or a rewritten command
